# Guardian project-level npm configuration.
#
# Redirects the npm download cache OUT of the repository directory.
# Rationale: in sandboxed development environments (Arena/Replit-style) the
# workspace directory is snapshot-persisted; npm's default cache (~/.npm)
# then accumulates thousands of files inside the persisted workspace and can
# exceed persistence budgets.
#
# IMPORTANT: use a DISK-BACKED location. /tmp is a RAM-backed tmpfs in many
# sandboxes — caching there consumes the very memory that installs and builds
# need (observed: ~1 GB tmpfs cache caused npm-ci OOM kills on a 2 GB host).
# /var/tmp is disk-backed on Linux and outside the persisted workspace.
#
# This is intentional, non-destructive, and safe to delete if you prefer the
# npm default cache location on your machine.
cache=/var/tmp/guardian-npm-cache
